194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186115292 1038 #edb/ref 17592186295201 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186115292 1038 #edb/ref 17592186295202 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186115292 1038 #edb/ref 17592186295203 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186115292 1038 #edb/ref 17592186295239 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186115292 1038 #edb/ref 17592186295240 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186115292 1038 #edb/ref 17592186295254 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186115342 1038 #edb/ref 17592186294986 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186115363 1038 #edb/ref 17592186295272 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186115366 1038 #edb/ref 17592186295273 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186115415 1038 #edb/ref 17592186294870 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186115653 1068 #edb/ref 17592186112854 13194139533410 17592186045585 false] [17592186115653 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294411 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186115653 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186115653 1071 "![](images/21/21eb95fdafee2b2bf33ef0857b889f992d5972cfcfa9545ba5b7c978956f9281.png)\n\nGiven $△ABC$ shown above, which of the following diagrams represents the height corresponding to $AB^(―)$?" 13194139533410 17592186045585 false] [17592186115653 1071 "![](images/21/21eb95fdafee2b2bf33ef0857b889f992d5972cfcfa9545ba5b7c978956f9281.png)\n\nGiven $△ABC$ shown above, which of the following diagrams represents the height corresponding to $\\overset{―}{AB}?$" 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186115653 1074 "The height (or altitude) corresponding to $\\overset{―}{AB}$ is a line segment that \n\n- runs from the opposite vertex $C$ to the line $\\overset{⟷}{AB},$ and\n\n- is perpendicular to $\\overset{⟷}{AB}.$\n\nTo draw the height, we proceed as follows:\n\n- Extend the line segment $\\overset{―}{AB}.$\n\n![](images/eb/eba964fd799b57b787ab20955b8717b02219ed785d2455cb122e08c448b43563.png)\n\n- Draw the perpendicular from $C$ to $\\overset{⟷}{AB}.$\n\n![](images/ad/adc7bbe174cdc56b7146d85bdec6e568e2cf829a3a64c73f6555e62c168c2eeb.png)" 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186115661 1068 #edb/ref 17592186112902 13194139533410 17592186045585 false] [17592186115661 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294171 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186115661 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186115661 1071 "![](images/81/812e1c08b671e54023a65dc5b9fbf089ddd27781ad555d6fb9e4d2a9816d193f.png)\n\nConsider the triangle $△ABC$ shown above. The line segment $AH^(―)$ is the altitude corresponding to $BC^(―)$. If $m∠ACB = 125^{∘}$, calculate $m∠HAC$." 13194139533410 17592186045585 false] [17592186115661 1071 "![](images/81/812e1c08b671e54023a65dc5b9fbf089ddd27781ad555d6fb9e4d2a9816d193f.png)\n\nConsider the triangle $△ABC$ shown above. The line segment $\\overset{―}{AH}$ is the altitude corresponding to $\\overset{―}{BC}.$ If $m∠ACB={125}^{∘},$ calculate $m∠HAC.$" 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186115661 1074 "Since the straight angle must have a measure of ${180}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠HCA+m∠ACB & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HCA+{125}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HCA & ={55}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $△AHC$ is a right triangle. Since its interior angles must sum to ${180}^{∘},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m∠HCA+m∠HAC+m∠AHC & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ {55}^{∘}+m∠HAC+{90}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HAC+{145}^{∘} & ={180}^{∘} \\\\ m∠HAC & ={35}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186115675 1068 #edb/ref 17592186112986 13194139533410 17592186045585 false] [17592186115675 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294748 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186115675 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186115675 1071 "A quadratic equation in the variable $x$ with real coefficients has a root $x =-1 + \\textrm{i}$. Given that the coefficient of $x^{2}$ in the equation is $1$, find the equation." 13194139533410 17592186045585 false] [17592186115675 1071 "A quadratic equation in the variable $x$ with real coefficients has a root $x=-1+\\text{i}.$ Given that the coefficient of ${x}^{2}$ in the equation is $1,$ find the equation." 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186115675 1074 "Since the quadratic equation has real coefficients and $x=-1+\\text{i}$ is a root, its conjugate $x=-1-\\text{i}$ must also be a root. Therefore, using the zero product property, we can write a quadratic equation with the required roots as follows:\n\n$$\n(x-(-1+\\text{i}))(x-(-1-\\text{i}))=0\n$$\n\nBy expanding the parentheses, we can write the equation in standard form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-x(-1+\\text{i})-x(-1-\\text{i})+(-1+\\text{i})(-1-\\text{i}) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+x-x\\text{i}+x+x\\text{i}+1-{\\text{i}}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2x+1+1 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2x+2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186115681 1068 #edb/ref 17592186113022 13194139533410 17592186045585 false] [17592186115681 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294634 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186115681 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186115681 1071 "![](images/43/434c2ac4c8b4043ad191bf23eff129ba79b26b0b7b838df4658df639ba140504.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{2},$ calculate the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above." 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186115681 1071 "![](images/43/434c2ac4c8b4043ad191bf23eff129ba79b26b0b7b838df4658df639ba140504.png)\n\nGiven that $\\sin θ = \\frac{1}{2}$, calculate the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above." 13194139533410 17592186045585 false] [17592186115681 1074 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{2},$ where $\\theta =m∠A.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ opposite to $∠A.$ Hence, we can use the sine ratio to find the length of the hypotenuse $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & =\\frac{8}{AB} \\\\ AB & =8(2) \\\\ AB & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use the Pythagorean Theorem to find the missing side $AC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\sqrt{A{B}^{2}-B{C}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{16}^{2}-{8}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{256-64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{192} \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8\\cdot (8\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =32\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186115682 1068 #edb/ref 17592186113028 13194139533410 17592186045585 false] [17592186115682 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294113 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186115682 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186115682 1071 "![](images/48/48cb6a248ab3ce706f26dc2e84e2feb337d509041c8b9756ea32fb3817aa097f.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=5,$ calculate the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above." 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186115682 1071 "![](images/48/48cb6a248ab3ce706f26dc2e84e2feb337d509041c8b9756ea32fb3817aa097f.png)\n\nGiven that $\\tan (m∠A) = 5$, calculate the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above." 13194139533410 17592186045585 false] [17592186115682 1074 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=5.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ 5 & =\\frac{2x+4}{x-1} \\\\ 5(x-1) & =2x+4 \\\\ 5x-5 & =2x+4 \\\\ 3x & =9 \\\\ x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =2x+4=2(3)+4=10, \\\\ AC & =x-1=3-1=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 10 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186115683 1068 #edb/ref 17592186113034 13194139533410 17592186045585 false] [17592186115683 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294185 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186115683 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186115683 1071 "![](images/7d/7dc806c646f1e9f5edbfef789fbdc9dfca2745c637906bd61eccb8072440e8c0.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to one decimal place, find the area of $△ABC$ shown above." 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186115683 1071 "![](images/7d/7dc806c646f1e9f5edbfef789fbdc9dfca2745c637906bd61eccb8072440e8c0.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to one decimal place, find the area of $△ABC$ shown above.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." 13194139533410 17592186045585 false] [17592186115683 1074 "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m∠A={63}^{∘}.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({63}^{∘}) & =\\frac{3x+2}{3x} \\\\ 3x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({63}^{∘}) & =3x+2 \\\\ 3x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({63}^{∘})-3x & =2 \\\\ 3x(\\operatorname{tan}⁡({63}^{∘})-1) & =2 \\\\ x & =\\frac{2}{3(\\operatorname{tan}⁡({63}^{∘})-1)} \\\\ x & =0.692\\,5…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =3x+2=3(0.692\\,5…)+2=4.077\\,6…, \\\\ AC & =3x=3(0.692\\,5…)=2.077\\,6….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}(2.077\\,6…)(4.077\\,6…) \\\\  & =4.236\\,0… \\\\  & ≈4.2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the one decimal place." 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186119882 1038 #edb/ref 17592186294878 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186129308 1038 #edb/ref 17592186294849 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186129308 1038 #edb/ref 17592186294850 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186129308 1038 #edb/ref 17592186294851 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186129308 1038 #edb/ref 17592186294853 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186129309 1038 #edb/ref 17592186294856 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186129309 1038 #edb/ref 17592186294857 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186129309 1038 #edb/ref 17592186294858 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186129309 1038 #edb/ref 17592186294859 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186129309 1038 #edb/ref 17592186294861 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186129310 1038 #edb/ref 17592186294862 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186129310 1038 #edb/ref 17592186294863 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186129310 1038 #edb/ref 17592186294864 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186129310 1038 #edb/ref 17592186294865 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186129310 1038 #edb/ref 17592186294866 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186129310 1038 #edb/ref 17592186294867 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186133942 1038 #edb/ref 17592186295204 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186133943 1038 #edb/ref 17592186295221 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186133943 1038 #edb/ref 17592186295222 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186133944 1038 #edb/ref 17592186295223 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186133944 1038 #edb/ref 17592186295224 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186133944 1038 #edb/ref 17592186295225 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186133945 1038 #edb/ref 17592186295250 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [