\\\ {x}^{2}-{3}^{2} & \\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve this inequality using familiar methods:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-{3}^{2} & \\ge 0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & \\ge {3}^{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & \\ge \\sqrt{{3}^{2}} \\\\ |x| & \\ge 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the inequality above is  $x\\le -3$ or $x\\ge 3.$" 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186294980 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294359 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186294980 1069 "q-278290" 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186294980 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186294980 1071 "![](images/36/36aeda6b6f5ce46552f55f458da60ef46a646d737c452d586389c03c47d1c9cb.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OF}=f,$ $\\overset{\\to }{OG}=g$ and $P$ divides $\\overset{―}{FG}$ in the ratio $FP:PG=8:5.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{OP}.$" 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186294980 1072 #uuid "06f1ebce-2b40-5089-bfea-ee16e90ad214" 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186294980 1074 "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OP}=\\overset{\\to }{OF}+\\overset{\\to }{FP}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OF}=f,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{FP}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OFG,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{FG} & =\\overset{\\to }{FO}+\\overset{\\to }{OG} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OF}+\\overset{\\to }{OG} \\\\  & =-f+g \\\\  & =g-f.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $FP:PG=8:5,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{FP}=\\frac{8}{13}\\overset{\\to }{FG}=\\frac{8}{13}(g-f).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OP} & =\\overset{\\to }{OF}+\\overset{\\to }{FP} \\\\  & =f+\\frac{8}{13}(g-f) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{13}f+\\frac{8}{13}g.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186294981 1068 #edb/ref 17592186293976 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186294981 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294329 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [175921862949