ength $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(2,-2),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=2,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=1.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-2))^{2}}{{1}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{4}+(y+2)^{2} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186295020 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294285 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186295020 1069 "q-278478" 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186295020 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186295020 1071 "![](images/59/591bf01f325ca1af8ffc34cb6c650cdf9024cf5dc672d9aed243723c476d7119.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186295020 1072 #uuid "4107a415-97f6-5414-80ab-675495103942" 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186295020 1074 "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(1,-3),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=4,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=2.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{{4}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-3))^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y+3)^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186295021 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294821 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186295021 1069 "q-278480" 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186295021 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533410 17592186045585 true] [17592186295021 1071 "![](images/c